# Social Follow
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: Social — a many-to-many relationship: any user may follow any user
# Case 11 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
#
# Note: this Machine has no natural single "owner" the way Item Unit Conversion
# belonged to Item, or Journal Entry Line belonged to Journal Entry. A Follow
# row belongs equally to a Follower and a Followee — the many-to-many shape
# CAP-F13 (one-directional reference) and CAP-F16 (parent-owned child table)
# don't name. This is the finding this case exists to surface.

Follow

Fields

- Follower : User
- Followee : User
- Followed At : Date

Constraints

- Follower is required.
- Followee is required.

    A Follower may follow a given Followee only once.

Permissions

Member

- Follow
- Unfollow

Views

- My Following : List
- My Followers : List
